Fixes #557.

## Problem
Runtime RC run `35938607692` rejected the successful Qwen 1.0.10 package from `2579f7ec...` with `AUTO_RUNTIME_CONTRACT_DRIFT` after main advanced only by acceptance/test tooling. The old fence compared the entire `local-companion` tree, so harmless test changes invalidated multi-GB runtime artifacts even when runtime inputs were unchanged.

## Change
- keep source ancestry/run/artifact identity checks unchanged;
- replace the broad `local-companion` drift fence with family-specific runtime input sets;
- derive CI policy coverage from the actual `push.paths` of Qwen/Whisper build workflows;
- print only changed runtime-contract paths on a real drift failure;
- document the contract in `qwen-runtime-package.yml`, intentionally refreshing an exact-source Qwen 1.0.10 Actions artifact on this final technical tree.

## Final-tree role
This PR is intentionally rebased on top of #553 / `main@273a6fd1fde3f3e269b63a4f046c05313525cdd3` and is planned as the last technical PR before real acceptance.

Because it changes both:
- a `local-companion/tests` policy file (causing the normal Companion Windows artifact to be built), and
- `.github/workflows/qwen-runtime-package.yml` (causing the Qwen bundle to be built),

the PR provides Companion + Qwen artifacts from the same integrated candidate tree for the later isolated physical gate.

## Acceptance
- CI + CodeQL green;
- Qwen Runtime Package green for this exact head/integrated PR tree;
- broad test/harness-only Companion changes no longer invalidate runtime RCs;
- real runtime input drift remains fail-closed;
- after merge, current-main/Production stays green.

Authenticode is deliberately not part of this gate per owner sequencing.

