## Why

The first full Rar GovDocs1 production run (35950421677) proved the historical S3-prefix enumerator is no longer a valid live acquisition path: all 1000 directory requests returned without transport errors, but `objects_seen=0` and `pub_extension_candidates=0`. That is a resolver failure, not a meaningful zero-PUB result.

Current DigitalCorpora documentation still exposes GovDocs1 as 1000 numbered ZIP bundles (000.zip..999.zip). This repair targets that documented distribution directly.

## Scope

- HTTP Range reads only the EOCD + central directory of each official ZIP;
- selects .pub members without downloading the full 200–400 MiB bundle;
- fetches only selected member local-header + compressed byte ranges;
- supports stored/deflate members, CRC and size verification;
- path-safety and encrypted-member rejection;
- classifies recovered bytes with the shared Rar Publisher classifier;
- quarantine remains mandatory;
- no raw member bytes are uploaded as public artifacts.

PR smoke indexes 000.zip and 001.zip. Main push scans all 1000 bundles with 16 workers.

## Priority 3 follow-up hardening

Inspection of PR #84 found that enum lookalikes were correctly blocked, but the exported planning mapper still trusted the remaining TypeScript field shapes. A malformed runtime record could therefore reach `clean()`/string operations before a controlled validation failure, or let a forged company identity shape bypass the intended boundary.

## Scope

- reconstruct planning company identity from runtime record evidence;
- require company name to be a string and optional company number/domain to be string/null/undefined only;
- reconstruct planning application candidates before any string/date/source handling;
- require application reference, description, status, received timestamp and source URL to be actual strings;
- require optional applicant name/site address to be string/null/undefined only;
- keep source tier and match basis on the reviewed runtime allowlists;
- add regression coverage for malformed record fields and company identity lookalikes;
- preserve authoritative-vs-aggregate provenance, exact-applicant verification, inference-only address matching and no-write/no-outreach locks.

## Safety / stack handling

Pure fail-closed TypeScript validation and tests. No live planning crawl, Supabase/CRM write, database migration, Apollo execution, credentials, provider activation, spend, customer communication or production deployment.

This PR is stacked on #84 and targets `fix/planning-runtime-enum-boundary`, not `main`. #84 should not advance on its historical green head until this child hardening is independently reviewed/accepted and #84 is reverified on the resulting exact head.

## Verification evidence

Exact head `06f0f6983bafb1876463f5445f0a86ca3fb6c22d`:

- Factory 041 deterministic gate run #203 — PASS;
- FEH Loop Engineering run #108 — PASS.

The verifier paths include Factory 041/044/045 focused tests, authentication, CRM navigation/SEO checks where applicable, execution-dispatch regression coverage, TypeScript typecheck, lint, and the accepted application-security drift guard.

## Human gate

Ready for independent review of this feature-branch hardening only. Dominic is requested. After human acceptance into #84's branch, #84 must rerun both verifiers on its refreshed exact head before returning to ready-for-review. Automation must not merge this PR, #84, or downstream reconciliation/consolidation PRs to `main`.

